============================================================================================
 READING
============================================================================================
 If ORDERS>=3 vanish for j<=3, then cap = O0+O1+O2 = pairwise truncation, and the only task is the
 CLOSED FORM of ORDER_2 (the total pairwise overlap) = C(j,2)/91. Then cap = 1 - j/7 + C(j,2)/91 =
 C(14-j,2)/91 SYMBOLICALLY (k>=10). The DIP at j=4,5 = the first nonvanishing ORDERS>=3 (triple/quad).
